{"authored" [{"question" "q-280531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A car accelerates from the origin with an acceleration of $(3i-4j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $2i\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the distance from the car to the origin$(|r|)$ after $4$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-280531/review.json" "file_sha256" "04c11e6ffe66f7c9242a9d74e462513a6905c72dd79cebe070cbcb404189da54" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-280531/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "5f8bffa6af32b6e1b67f239f6d6ae9ab71f7137140ff46a8c2d86c5a385ec1ca" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-280531/verification.json" "basis" 1428 "rationale" "The original prompt says from rest while also specifying nonzero initial velocity2i m/s. These assumptions are inconsistent: literal rest yields40m, whereas the explicit velocity yields32sqrt2m. The site revealed a worked solution using u=2i and concluding32sqrt2. The authorized local repair removes only from rest in the study prompt and supplies a consistent locally written solution. The original DOM, screenshot, uncertain solver answer, both mathematical interpretations, site grading and revealed solution remain separate, unchanged evidence. New field and answer identities preserve historical definitions."} {"question" "q-280531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "With constant acceleration, the position is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\mathbf r_0+\\mathbf u t+\\tfrac12\\mathbf a t^2.\n$$\n\nHere $\\mathbf r_0=\\mathbf0$, $\\mathbf u=2\\mathbf i\\,\\mathrm{m/s}$, and $\\mathbf a=(3\\mathbf i-4\\mathbf j)\\,\\mathrm{m/s^2}$. At $t=4\\,\\mathrm{s}$,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r(4)&=\\mathbf0+(2\\mathbf i)(4)+\\tfrac12(3\\mathbf i-4\\mathbf j)(4^2)\\\\\n&=8\\mathbf i+24\\mathbf i-32\\mathbf j\\\\\n&=(32\\mathbf i-32\\mathbf j)\\,\\mathrm m.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe distance to the origin is therefore\n\n$$\n|\\mathbf r(4)|=\\sqrt{32^2+(-32)^2}=\\sqrt{2048}=\\boxed{32\\sqrt2\\,\\mathrm m}.\n$$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-280531/review.json" "file_sha256" "04c11e6ffe66f7c9242a9d74e462513a6905c72dd79cebe070cbcb404189da54" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-280531/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "5f8bffa6af32b6e1b67f239f6d6ae9ab71f7137140ff46a8c2d86c5a385ec1ca" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-280531/verification.json" "basis" 1428 "rationale" "The original prompt says from rest while also specifying nonzero initial velocity2i m/s. These assumptions are inconsistent: literal rest yields40m, whereas the explicit velocity yields32sqrt2m. The site revealed a worked solution using u=2i and concluding32sqrt2. The authorized local repair removes only from rest in the study prompt and supplies a consistent locally written solution. The original DOM, screenshot, uncertain solver answer, both mathematical interpretations, site grading and revealed solution remain separate, unchanged evidence. New field and answer identities preserve historical definitions."} {"question" "q-280531" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "32\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-280531/review.json" "file_sha256" "04c11e6ffe66f7c9242a9d74e462513a6905c72dd79cebe070cbcb404189da54" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-280531/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "5f8bffa6af32b6e1b67f239f6d6ae9ab71f7137140ff46a8c2d86c5a385ec1ca" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-280531/verification.json" "basis" 1428 "rationale" "The original prompt says from rest while also specifying nonzero initial velocity2i m/s. These assumptions are inconsistent: literal rest yields40m, whereas the explicit velocity yields32sqrt2m. The site revealed a worked solution using u=2i and concluding32sqrt2. The authorized local repair removes only from rest in the study prompt and supplies a consistent locally written solution. The original DOM, screenshot, uncertain solver answer, both mathematical interpretations, site grading and revealed solution remain separate, unchanged evidence. New field and answer identities preserve historical definitions."} {"question" "q-136379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves from the origin with a constant velocity of  $(2i+5j)\\,\\text{cm/s}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $3$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\n \nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=2i+5j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(2i+5j)(3) \\\\  & =(6i+15j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136379" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136379" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-i+2j)\\,\\text{cm}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136379" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(5i+8j)\\,\\text{cm}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c9