er/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2i\\,\\text{km}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136375" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2j\\,\\text{km}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves with a constant velocity of $(6i+2j)\\,\\text{cm/s}.$ If its initial position is ${r}_{0}=(3i-5j)\\,\\text{cm},$ find its position vector $r$ after $5$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}  \n$i\\,\\,+$  \n{{field-2}}  \n$j)\\text{cm}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When a particle (or object) moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector at time $t$ is given by the equation\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position vector.\n\nIn this case,\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=3i-5j,\\,u=6i+2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=5\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(3i-5j)+(6i+2j)(5) \\\\  & =3i-5j+30i+10j \\\\  & =(\\,33\\,i+5\\,j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280488" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280488" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "33"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280488" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280488" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A bird glides with a constant velocity of $(-2i-1j)\\,\\text{yd/s}.$ If it starts at the position ${r}_{0}=(6i+4j)\\,\\text{yd},$ find its position vector $r$ after $3$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}  \n$i\\,\\,+$  \n{{field-2}}  \n$j)\\text{yd}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When a particle (or object) moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector at time $t$ is given by the equation\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position vector.\n\nIn this case,\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=6i+4j,\\,u=-2i-1j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the bird after $t=3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(6i+4j)+(-2i-1j)(3) \\\\  & =6i+4j-6i-3j \\\\  & =(\\,0\\,i+1\\,j)\\,\\text{yd}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280491" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280491" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "An autonomous submarine travels with a constant velocity of $(3i+5j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$ If its initial position is ${r}_{0}=(-3i+0j)\\,\\text{km},$ find the position vector $r$ after $3$ hours.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}  \n$i\\,\\,+$  \n{{field-2}}  \n$j)\\text{km}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When a particle (or object) moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector at time $t$ is given by the equation\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position vector.\n\nIn this case,\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=-3i+0j,\\,u=3i+5j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the submarine after $t=3\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(-3i+0j)+(3i+5j)(3) \\\\  & =-3i+0j+9i+15j \\\\  & =(\\,6\\,i+15\\,j)\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280492" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/re