\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{m}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=-3i+2j,\\,u=5i-2j,\\,a=2i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the skier after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(-3i+2j)+(5i-2j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(2i+j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(-3i+2j)+(5i-2j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(8i+4j) \\\\  & =(-3i+2j)+(10i-4j)+(4i+2j) \\\\  & =(\\,11\\,i+0\\,j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280513" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-