verification.json"} {"question" "q-136413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(4i-7j)\\,\\text{mm}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(9i-64j)\\,\\text{mm}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(9i-64j)\\,\\text{mm}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A mail truck departs from the post office at the origin and drives with a constant velocity of $(4i-3j)\\,\\text{mi/h}.$ Determine the distance $(|r|)$ from the truck to the origin after $2$ hours.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{mi}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=4i-3j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the truck after $t=2\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(4i-3j)(2) \\\\  & =(8i-6j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the truck to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|8i-6j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280526" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280526" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A car accelerates from rest at the origin with an acceleration of $(3i-4j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $2i\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the distance from the car to the origin$(|r|)$ after $4$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=2i,\\,a=3i-4j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the car after $t=4\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(2i)(4)+\\frac{1}{2}(3i-4j)(4)^{2} \\\\  & =8i+8(3i-4j) \\\\  & =8i+24i-32j \\\\  & =(32i-32j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the car to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|32i-32j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(32)^{2}+(-32)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1024+1024} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2048} \\\\  & =32\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A cyclist begins at the position $(2i-j)\\,\\text{m}$ with an initial velocity of $(3i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ and an acceleration of $(i+2j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Find the distance from the cyclist to the origin $(|r|)$ after $2$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=2i-j,\\,u=3i+j,\\,a=i+2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the cyclist after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(2i-j)+(3i+j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+2j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(2i-j)+(6i+2j)+2(i+2j) \\\\  & =(2i-j)+(6i+2j)+(2i+4j) \\\\  & =(10i+5j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the cyclist to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|10i+5j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{125} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280535" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280535" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(2i-4j)\\,\\text{m},$ with an acceleration of $(-i+j)\\,{\\text{m/min}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(3i-j)\\,\\text{m/min}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $6$ minutes." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=2i-4j,\\,u=3i-j,\\,a=-i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=6\\,\\text{min}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(2i-4j)+(3i-j)(6)+\\frac{1}{2}(-i+j)(6)^{2} \\\\  & =(2i-4j)+(18i-6j)+18(-i+j) \\\\  & =(20i-10j)+(-18i+18j) \\\\  & =(2i+8j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|2i+8j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{68} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{17}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136437" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136437" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "14\\,\\text{m}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136437" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{17}\\,\\text{m}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/1