" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{8}\\,\\text{cm}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{cm}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(3\\mathbf{j} - \\mathbf{i}) \\: \\textrm{mi}$ with a constant velocity of $(\\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j}) \\: \\textrm{mi/h}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $2$ hours." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/example-9821.json" "file_sha256" "a2884f8378942210530d39d7cd0ad120094a6501b2051e76565fd92a206d96ad" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $\\mathbf{u},$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + \\mathbf{u} t,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $\\mathbf{r}_0$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}_0 = 3\\mathbf{j} - \\mathbf{i}, \\qquad \\mathbf u = \\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t = 2 \\: \\textrm{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(3j-i)+(i-j)(2) \\\\  & =(-i+3j)+(2i-2j) \\\\  & =(i+j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/example-9821.json" "file_sha256" "a2884f8378942210530d39d7cd0ad120094a6501b2051e76565fd92a206d96ad" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(4\\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j})\\,\\textrm{cm}$ with an acceleration of $(\\mathbf{i} + 3\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{cm/min}^2$ and an initial velocity of $(\\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j}) \\: \\textrm{cm/min}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $4$ minutes." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/example-9822.json" "file_sha256" "b943d2412939b38e9e1607958847e16639fbdb98ff7cd1e5219957b4f6bcfefd" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $\\mathbf{a},$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + \\mathbf{u} t + \\dfrac12 \\mathbf{a} t^2,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}_0$ is the initial position of the particle and $\\mathbf{u}$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}_0 = 4\\mathbf i - \\mathbf j , \\qquad \\mathbf u = \\mathbf{i} +\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad \\mathbf a = \\mathbf{i} + 3\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t = 4 \\, \\textrm{min}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(4i-j)+(i+j)(4)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+3j)(4)^{2} \\\\  & =(4i-j)+(4i+4j)+8(i+3j) \\\\  & =(8i+3j)+(8i+24j) \\\\  & =(16i+27j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/example-9822.json" "file_sha256" "b943d2412939b38e9e1607958847e16639fbdb98ff7cd1e5219957b4f6bcfefd" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves from the origin with an acceleration of $(\\mathbf{i} +\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{cm/s}^2$ and an initial velocity of $(-\\mathbf{i}-2\\mathbf{j}) \\: \\textrm{cm/s}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $6$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/example-9824.json" "file_sha256" "a58999a635ea69a847c02eb4b4fe6bbb9b83615d2d06156089bcc30349b40b8d" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $\\mathbf{a},$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + \\mathbf{u} t + \\dfrac12 \\mathbf{a} t^2,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}_0$ is the initial position of the particle and $\\mathbf{u}$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}_0 = 0\\mathbf i +0 \\mathbf j , \\qquad \\mathbf u = -\\mathbf{i}-2\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad \\mathbf a = \\mathbf{i} +\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t = 6 \\, \\textrm{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(-i-2j)(6)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+j)(6)^{2} \\\\  & =(-6i-12j)+18(i+j) \\\\  & =(-6i-12j)+(18i+18j) \\\\  & =(12i+6j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|12i+6j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{180} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/example-9824.json" "file_sha256" "a58999a635ea69a847c02eb4b4fe6bbb9b83615d2d06156089bcc30349b40b8d" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [] "usage" {"q-136375" [] "q-136379" [] "q-136416" [] "q-136436" [] "q-280488" [] "q-280531" [] "q-280492" [] "q-280504" [] "q-280513" [] "q-136413" [] "q-280507" [] "q-280535" [] "e-9824" [] "e-9821" [] "e-9822" [] "q-280526" [] "q-136437" [] "q-280491" []} "basis" 1428 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186306638 17592186306639 17592186306640 17592186306641 17592186306642 17592186306645 17592186306646 17592186306647 17592186306648 17592186306649 17592186306651 17592186306652 17592186306653 17592186306654 17592186306655 17592186306658 17592186306659 17592186306660 17592186306661 17592186306662 17592186306665 17592186306666 17592186306667 17592186306668 17592186306669 17592186306672 17592186306673 17592186306674 17592186306675 17592186306676 17592186306679 17592186306681 17592186306684 17592186306685 17592186306687 17592186306690 17592186306692 17592186306695 17592186306697 17592186306700 17592186306701 17592186306703 17592186306706 17592186306708 17592186306711 17592